    "text": "<p>Acidic strength<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8733;</mo></math> Stability of conjugate base General Order of acidic strength:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>COOH</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>Ph</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>OH</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi>CH</mi></math><br />&#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&#39; is more acidic due to<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> effect of<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> .</p><p>Hence , order of acidic strength is: b&gt;c&gt;d&gt;a</p>",
